BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Berta Rojas\, Paraguayan Guitarist | HumanArts
DTSTART:20261007T190000
DTEND:20261007T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T174442Z
UID:e9b9d022556927b97177305e29dd55@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:October 7\, 2026\, 7:00 PM\, TFAC Curtis Performance Hall In a
 ssociation with National Hispanic Heritage Month\, Latin American Grammy-w
 inning guitarist Berta Rojas will discuss her recent project and publicati
 on\, La Huella de las Cuerdas (The Journey of Strings). Presented across v
 arious formats—vinyl\, streaming\, videos\, and book with innovative aug
 mented reality—it traces the intriguing story of how the guitars and vih
 uelas brought to Latin America by the conquistadors influenced the contine
 nt’s cultures and traditions and in turn was itself transformed\, giving
  rise to unique instruments that voice the soul of the region’s people a
 nd their identities. Fellow author and guitarist Mark Small will mediate t
 he discussion\, which will also include live performance. Source: Assumpti
 on University Event page: https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/event
 s/berta-rojas-paraguayan-guitarist-humanarts\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 
 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from worcester
 -colleges-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-eve
 nts/events/berta-rojas-paraguayan-guitarist-humanarts
LOCATION:Curtis Performance Hall\, Tsotsis Family Academic Center\, 500 Sa
 lisbury Street\, Worcester\, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.assumption.edu/news-and-events/events/berta-rojas-paraguay
 an-guitarist-humanarts
END:VEVENT
