DESCRIPTION:Join us as we celebrate Indigenous Peoples’ Day in community
 . This year\, we’re centering the histories and stories of the native pl
 ants that reside in our Courtyard and gardens\, allowing us to acknowledge
  the indigenous soil from which they grow and the original and current ste
 wards of the land upon which the Museum resides. The Gardner Museum is hon
 ored to collaborate with: • Hawk Henries—artist\, composer\, and flute
  musician of the Chaubunagungamaug band of Nipmuck • Malissa Costa (Mash
 pee Wampanoag)—Plimoth Patuxet Museums Associate Director of Indigenous 
