BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Choir concert: Tõnu Kõrvits\, composer
DTSTART:20261025T190000
DTEND:20261025T200000
DTSTAMP:20261006T174442Z
UID:e228a8293c407aeaf497721f029db6@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The Holy Cross College Choir will be performing a program of m
 usic from Scandinavia and the Baltics\, featuring Kreek’s Notebook by Aw
 ard-winning Estonian composer Tõnu Kõrvits. Estonia has a rich tradition
  of choral music. The country plays host to the Estonian Song Festival\, w
 hich started in 1869 and currently runs every five years\, is one of the l
 argest singing festivals in the world\, welcoming over 100\,000 people com
 ing together to unite in song. Kreek’s Notebook celebrates the rich heri
 tage of Estonian Choral Music through the use of native folk hymns collect
 ed by ethnomusicologist Cyrillus Kreek (1889–1962). Korvits weaves sacre
 d folk hymns and texts collected by Kreek into his own distinct musical la
 nguage. A multi-movement work for string orchestra and choir\, Kreek’s N
 otebook synthesizes traditional melodies with thrilling avant-garde string
  writing\, inviting the listener into moments of spiritual contemplation a
 nd visceral passion. Additional works on the program include music by Arvo
  Pärt\, Veljo Tormis\, Algirdas Martinaitis\, and Laura Jekabsone. Funded
  by The Patrick E. Moriarty\, M.D. '57 Visiting Scholars Program. Dress Co
